ive integers with\n\n$$\nx \\leq 10\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\ny \\leq 12\n$$\n\nis given by\n\n$$\n|X|-|A\\cup B|=171 - 43 =128.\n$$" 13194139541978 17592186576411 false] [17592186157221 1074 "Recall that the hexadecimal integers $\\textrm{A}-\\textrm{F}$ correspond to decimal integers $10-15{:}$\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\textrm{A}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\textrm{B}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\textrm{C}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\textrm{D}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\textrm{E}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$\\textrm{F}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$11$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$12$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$13$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$14$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$15$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nTo write a hexadecimal integer as the corresponding binary number, we convert each digit of the hexadecimal number into a $4$-digit binary (with leading zeros if necessary) and concatenate the results.\n\n- Converting each digit of $(\\textrm{FE}9)_{16}$ into binary, we obtain:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{F} & =15={2}^{3}+{2}^{2}+{2}^{1}+{2}^{0}=(1111)_{2} \\\\ \\text{E} & =14={2}^{3}+{2}^{2}+{2}^{1}=(1110)_{2} \\\\ 9 & ={2}^{3}+{2}^{0}=(1001)_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n- Concatenating the results, we get\n$(\\textrm{FE}9)_{16} = (1111 \\: 1110 \\: 1001)_2$." 13194139541978 17592186576411 true] [17592186157221 1074 "Recall that the hexadecimal integers $\\textrm{A}-\\textrm{F}$ correspond to decimal integers $10-15{:}$\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\