nt II is false. Since $f'(x) \\ngeq 0$ for all $x > 1$, the sequence $a_n$ is *not* increasing.\n- Statement III is false. Since $f'(x) \\nleq 0$ for all $x > 1$, the sequence $a_n$ is *not* decreasing.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\"" 13194139541978 17592186576411 false] [17592186184122 1074 "We wish to express $\\sin 860^\\circ$ in terms of $\\sin\\theta_R$, where $\\theta_R$ is the reference angle corresponding to the angle\n\n$$\n\\theta = 860^\\circ\n$$\n\nTo express $\\sin 860^\\circ$ in terms of $\\sin\\theta_R$, we proceed as follows:\n\n- **Step 1:** Find an angle that's coterminal with $860^\\circ$ that lies in the range $[0, 360^\\circ)$. We do this by subtracting integer multiples of $360^\\circ$ until we get our desired angle:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{860}^{∘}-{360}^{∘} & ={500}^{∘} \\\\ {860}^{∘}-2\\cdot {360}^{∘} & ={140}^{∘}\\hspace{1em}{\\color{green}{✓}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\nTherefore,\n$\\sin 860^\\circ = \\sin 140^\\circ$.\n\n![](images/8c/8c3331f0b9d99cc20d68ee87aa473cfa5ec27b64a12b446ad90d128a90a4051c.png)\n\n- **Step 2**: Compute the reference angle. Since $\\theta = 140^\\circ$ is in the $2$nd quadrant, the reference angle is\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\theta_R = 180^\\circ - 140^\\circ= 40^\\circ.\n$$\n- **Step 3**: Determine the correct sign. The sine function is positive $({\\color{blue}{+}})$ in the second quadrant. Therefore,\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\sin (860^\\circ) = {\\color{blue}{+}}\\sin\\theta_R = {\\color{blue}{+}}\\sin{40^\\circ}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\sin 860^\\circ = \\sin 40^\\circ\n$$" 13194139541978 17592186576411 true] [17592186184122 1074 "We wish to express $\\sin 860^\\circ$ in terms of $\\sin\\theta_R$, where $\\theta_R$ is the reference angle corresponding to the angle\n\n$$\n\\theta = 860^\\circ\n$$\n\nTo express $\\sin 860^\\circ$ in terms of $\\sin\\theta_R$, we proceed as follows:\n\n- **Step 1:** Find an angle that's coterminal with $860^\\circ$ that lies in the range $[0,