 \\\\\ny &= -\\frac{20}{3} - \\frac{2}{3}x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we’ll analyze each of the given values of $x$ in turn.\n\n- Consider $x = 0$.\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-\\frac{20}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}(0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{20}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n- Consider $x = 3$.\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-\\frac{20}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}(3) \\\\  & =-\\frac{20}{3}-2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{26}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n- Consider $x = 6$.\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-\\frac{20}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}(6) \\\\  & =-\\frac{20}{3}-4 \\\\  & =-\\frac{32}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the table is the following:\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\displaystyle -\\dfrac{20}{3}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\displaystyle -\\dfrac{26}{3}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\displaystyle -\\dfrac{32}{3}$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n" 13194139541978 17592186576411 true] [17592186208307 1074 "To write the table, we first express $y$ as a function of $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{3}{4}y &= -5 - \\frac{1}{2}x \\\\\ny &= \\frac{4}{3}(-5 - \\frac{1}{2}x) \\\\\ny &= -\\frac{20}{3} - \\frac{2}{3}x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we’ll analyze each of the given values of $x$ in turn.\n\n- Consider $x = 0$.\n$$\n\\displaystyle y|=-\\frac{20}{3} - \\frac{2}{3}(0); =-\\frac{20}{3}\n$$\n- Consider $x = 3$.\n$$\n\\displaystyle y|=-\\frac{20}{3} - \\frac{2}{3}(3); =-\\frac{20}{3} - 2; =-\\frac{26}{3}\n$$\n- Consider $x = 6$.\n$$\n\\displaystyle y|=-\\frac{20}{3} - \\frac{2}{3}(6); =-\\frac{20}